Package: amber-glycin
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Andre Bremer <hyperquader@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: @DEPS@, bubblewrap, amber-gtk4 (>= @GTK_MIN@)
Section: libs
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/Hyperquader-Coders/amber-glycin
Description: glycin image-loading runtime bundle for the amber suite
 One glycin build shared by the amber applications, installed to
 /usr/lib/amber-glycin and reached only through those applications'
 RUNPATH. It is deliberately not on the ldconfig path, so installing it
 cannot change what anything else on the system links against.
 .
 glycin decodes images in sandboxed loader processes (bubblewrap and
 seccomp) and hands the pixels back through a memfd. The package holds
 libglycin-2, libglycin-gtk4-2, and the 2+ loaders with their config.
 Linux Mint ships only the 1+ loaders and no libglycin. Applications set
 GLYCIN_DATA_DIR to /usr/lib/amber-glycin/share before the first load.
 .
 This is a runtime bundle, not a development package. Headers and
 pkg-config files are not shipped.
